on these inputs. The first two are the published Keccak-256 vectors; the last two
were produced by an independently written pure-Python Keccak-256 that reproduces
the published pair.

`decide` here evaluates the whole sponge in the kernel; the list literals and the
padded messages also need a raised recursion limit for the elaborator's own
evaluation, so both options are set for the rest of the file. -/

set_option maxRecDepth 100000
set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000

